        "node_id": "n_8_6887e4",
        "thought_text": "Thought-2 (revised): Instead of using a recursive backtracking approach, which can be inefficient due to exploring all possible combinations, we can use a more efficient method. We can sort the scores in descending order and try to form two teams by iteratively adding the highest available scores to each team. If at any point the difference between the two team scores exceeds the remaining highest score, it's impossible to balance the teams, and we can return \"NO\". Otherwise, if we successfully form two teams with equal scores, we return \"YES\". This approach ensures that we efficiently find a solution if one exists.",
